W: 2. In jacket blue and trousers white,
W: Just like a sailor, neat and tight,
W: The great salt sea was the heart's delight,
W: Of the female rambling sailor.
W: From stem to stern she freely goes,
W: She braves all dangers, fears no foes,
W: But soon you will hear of the overthrow,
W: Of the female rambling sailor.
W:
W: 3. Though never did her courage fail,
W: T'was stormy seas and wintry gale,
W: O'er which this fair young maiden did prevail,
W: This female rambling sailor.
W: From stem to stern she freely went,
W: Where oftimes she'd been many
W: But her hand did slip and down she fell
W: She calmly bade this world farewell.
W:
W: 4. When her lily white breast in sight it came,
W: It appeared to be a female's frame,
W: Rebecca Young was the name,
W: Of the female rambling sailor.
W: May the willows wave all around her grave,
W: And round the laurels planted,
W: Roses sweet grow at the feet,
W: Of the one who was undaunted.
W:
W: 5. So, come all you maids, both near and far,
W: And listen to my story,
W: Her body is anchored in the ground,
W: Let's hope her soul is in glory.
W: On the river Thames she's known right well,
W: No sailor there could her excel,
W: Shed one tear in a last farewell
W: To the female rambling sailor.
%
